  "scope": "Proves global all-direction covariance ellipticity for the actual normalized SU(2) Haar tilt, with a literal original Wilson conditional-source binding. Proves a quantitative rectangle bound for interactions created by true compact Gibbs integration and binds it to computed generated factors. Proves that the prior positive contact majorant diverges if a subtracted stage reaches fixed physical radius; this is only an estimator obstruction. Supplies a stronger actual weighted-displacement sufficient criterion, without claiming its Wilson hypotheses. Preserves all larger-scale covariance kernels exactly: the sum of later actual noise kernels and final true covariance equals the earlier retained covariance. Existing growing ultraviolet contact errors vanish against this entire nonlocal package for arbitrary additional finite depth at each cutoff. A finite diagonal limit, if it exists, is nonnegative; no limit, strictly positive separated signal, reflected positivity, physical bracket signs or mass gap is thereby constructed. Also proves an actual aligned six-staple Haar-integral Gaussian approximation in fluctuation coordinates: the vacuum-subtracted potential differs from (5*x^2+5*y^2-2*x*y)/6 by at most (R^4/2+3*R^2/10)/beta for beta>=max(1,R^2), |x|,|y|<=R. This is one literal fiber integral, not an established full-lattice exterior realization or control of the subsequent induced tower.",
  "results": {
    "local_ellipticity": {
      "law": "Actual normalized quaternion Haar tilt exp(2*beta*inner(q,A)); no surrogate probability law.",
      "exact_decomposition": "Radial and tangent directions are covariance-orthogonal. For B perpendicular to A, kappa*Cov(B,B)=axisMean(kappa)*norm(B)^2, kappa=2*beta*norm(A).",
      "large_tilt": "kappa>=50 implies kappa^2*Cov(B,B)>=3*norm(B)^2/4 in every direction.",
      "all_tilts": "For beta>=0, (1+kappa)^2*Cov(B,B)>=exp(-100)*norm(B)^2/4. Small kappa uses an actual normalized Haar density comparison; large kappa uses the proved directional decomposition.",
      "wilson_binding": "The original Wilson six-staple bound norm(A)<=6 and exact conditional source variance give (1+12*beta)^2*Var_cond(source_f)>=exp(-100)*norm(B_f)^2, uniformly in exterior configuration.",
      "limits": "This is a local conditional-noise floor. B_f can vanish. It does not give a nonzero retained source, separated physical signal, or a bound for every later induced nonlinear action.",
      "wilson_domain": "Original periodic four-dimensional SU(2) Wilson lattice with period n>1, beta>=0 and every actual exterior configuration."
    },
    "induced_interaction": {
      "quantity": "F(A)=-log integral exp(-A) dmu with normalized actual compact reference probability.",
      "bound": "For explicit four fiber actions, |F(A11)-F(A10)-F(A01)+F(A00)| <= d+osc(A00-A10)*osc(A00-A01)/4 when the original mixed fiber action has sup norm<=d.",
      "binding": "The actual nextFactor (.inr e) generated by finite-factor elimination satisfies this same bound, with explicit pre-integration increments.",
      "limit": "This controls a true generated interaction but is not weak-coupling smallness. Bounds based only on original Wilson ranges can grow with beta."
    },
    "contact_barrier": {
      "exact": "a*R^4*c^9=R^4*(a*c)^9/a^8. More generally (c^4/a^4)*(c*a)^(N+1)=(a*c)^(N+5)/a^8.",
      "proved_obstruction": "If a tends to zero, R>=R0>0, stage costs are nonnegative, and any included physical radius a*c>=ell>0, the positive accumulated geometric factor tends to infinity, hence not zero.",
      "interpretation": "A diverging upper-bound expression does not imply a diverging actual covariance or remainder.",
      "replacement": "The literal Taylor subtraction error is bounded by seminorm_(0,N+1)(F)/N! times sum_j integral |K_j|*|displacement_j|^(N+1), assuming the stated integrability conditions. Vanishing moments imply vanishing subtraction error.",
      "limit": "The actual Wilson moment estimates and separate periodic tails have not been established at a fixed physical scale."
    },
    "coarse_package": {
      "exact": "Coarse(J,L)=a^-8*sum_{j=J}^{J+L-1} actualGram_j + a^-8*Cov_{J+L}=a^-8*Cov_J.",
      "physical_dictionary": "For real Schwartz tensors, every Gram term is the full original cell-sampled physical kernel pairing.",
      "growing_uv_repair": "On the previously proved UV path, full physical covariance minus contacts through k differs by o(1) from Coarse(k,L(k)) for every finite L(k). No extra smallness is asserted for the coarse kernels.",
      "positivity": "Diagonal Coarse>=0 and final diagonal covariance<=Coarse. If a finite repaired diagonal limit exists, it is nonnegative. No OS/reflection positivity or strict positivity follows.",
      "limit_equivalence": "A finite real repaired covariance limit exists with value c if and only if the corresponding nonlocal package tends to c. This retains the unsolved physical estimate explicitly."
    },
    "aligned_one_fiber_gaussian": {
      "law": "V_beta(t,s)=-log integral exp[-beta*(12-2*inner(q,4+rotor(t)+rotor(s)))] dHaar(q), rotor(t)=cos(t)+i*sin(t).",
      "radial_correction": "For beta>0 and 0<r<=6, |V_beta(r)-V_beta(6)-2*beta*(6-r)|<=3*(6-r)/(2*r).",
      "geometric_identity": "The six-staple norm satisfies r(t,s)^2=18+8*cos(t)+8*cos(s)+2*cos(t-s). A proved fourth-order cosine error controls the quadratic remainder.",
      "scaled_bound": "For beta>=max(1,R^2), |x|,|y|<=R: |V_beta(x/sqrt(beta),y/sqrt(beta))-V_beta(0,0)-(5*x^2+5*y^2-2*x*y)/6|<=(R^4/2+3*R^2/10)/beta.",
      "interpretation": "The leading cross interaction survives at order one in fluctuation coordinates; its nonlinear remainder becomes small for this actual centered star integral.",
      "limits": "No proof that these two independent rotating staples are realized by a common full-lattice exterior is included. This bounded-coordinate approximation does not prove a normalized Gaussian law on the whole plane, tightness, a multiscale induced-action remainder estimate, or a four-dimensional continuum limit.",
      "fixed_coordinate_limit": "The vacuum-subtracted scaled star potential is proved to tend to (5*x^2+5*y^2-2*x*y)/6 for every fixed x,y as real beta tends to infinity."
    }
  },
