      "status": "Natural mathematical argument only; not part of the Lean declaration certificate and not a Wilson covariance claim.",
      "construction": "For a fixed physical ball B, K_a(x,y)=a^-8*1_B(x)*1_B(y) is rank-one PSD, finite range and amplitude<=a^-8. Choose two nonnegative smooth compactly supported bumps f,g with disjoint closed supports inside B. Their tensor has all diagonal Taylor jets zero, while its kernel pairing is a^-8*(integral f)*(integral g), which diverges.",
